status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIYAMA, YASUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A packing container comprising a container body (12) and a lid body fused to the top wall (12a) of the container body and provided with an opening-carrying body portion and a rockably supported lid portion, wherein a spout portion provided on the top wall is formed with a breaking portion (23) which consists of a thin-walled portion (24) and a breaking line area (27) and, when the lid body is to be attached to the container body, at least the breaking line area adjacent to the thin-walled portion is bonded to the lower surface of the lid portion, whereby, when the lid portion is pulled up and turned, the breaking portion is broken to open the packing container.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un récipient: comportant un corps (12), un couvercle d'une pièce avec la paroi supérieure (12a) du corps, une partie du corps portant l'ouverture, et une partie de couvercle pivotante. Un orifice verseur situé dans la paroi supérieure est constitué d'une partie détachable (23) consistant en une paroi mince (24) entourée par une ligne de rupture (27). Si le couvercle est solidaire du corps, au moins la zone de la ligne de rupture voisine de la partie de paroi mince est collée à la surface inférieure du couvercle; ainsi lorsqu'on tire et tourne le couvercle la ligne de rupture se déchire en créant une ouverture.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>